<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan auctions 240.2 million rupees bonds.</title>
<headline>Pakistan auctions 240.2 million rupees bonds.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-02-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The State (central) Bank of Pakistan said it auctioned Federal Investment Bonds worth 240.2 million rupees on Sunday.</p>
<p>The three-year bonds worth 150.2 million rupees and 10-year bonds worth 90 million were accepted at par, the bank said.</p>
<p>Bids received totalled 240.2 million rupees, the bank said.</p>
<p>($1 = 40.22 rupees) -- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
